ikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_strike_campaign","source_date":"2025","inclusion_reason":"Absent from the base List parse; capacity per the Deep strike campaign table.","canonical_id":"slavyansk-eco","denominator_status":"member"},{"name":"TAIF-NK Refinery","operator":"TAIF-NK","capacity_mtpa":8.5,"region_code":"RU-TA","listed_under":"curated_supplement","source_page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_strike_campaign","source_date":"2025","inclusion_reason":"Nizhnekamsk refinery operated by TAIF-NK, DISTINCT from the Tatneft/TANECO Nizhnekamsk entry already in the base list. Capacity per the Deep strike campaign table.","canonical_id":"taif-nk","denominator_status":"member"},{"name":"Mari El Refinery","operator":"New Stream (Mariysky NPZ)","capacity_mtpa":1.2,"region_code":"RU-ME","listed_under":"curated_supplement","source_page":"https://www.abarrelfull.co.uk/Mari-El_Refinery","source_date":"2024","inclusion_reason":"Small refinery in Mari El absent from the base List parse; conservative current-throughput figure (~1.2 MTPA), not the expansion design capacity.","canonical_id":"mari-el","denominator_status":"mini"}],"total_mtpa":273.8,"reconciliation":{"national_public_estimate_mtpa":327.0,"national_estimate_source":"Carnegie Endowment (Oct 2025) + Reuters/industry consensus; ~6.5 mb/d nameplate","tracked_mtpa":273.8,"tracked_refineries":34,"coverage_pct":90.4,"gap_mtpa":53.2,"excluded_non_fuels":["Tobolsk Petrochemical Refinery"],"reference_nameplate_mtpa":327.0,"reference_range_mtpa":[320.0,330.0],"reference_crude_nameplate_mtpa":303.0,"reference_year":2025,"reference_definition":"Russia-only nameplate primary distillation (CDU-TEK basis), which INCLUDES gas-condensate splitters and mini-refineries. 2024 THROUGHPUT was ~267 MTPA — this is capacity, not throughput.","denominator_coverage_pct":90.4,"denominator_coverage_basis":"crude-fuels nameplate reference (~303 MTPA)","facility_count":34,"excluded_facility_count":1,"excluded_condensate_splitters":["Surgut Condensate Stabilization Plant (~12 MTPA, Gazprom; condensate, not crude)","Novatek Ust-Luga complex (~9 MTPA; stable gas condensate, not crude)","Astrakhan condensate refining line (~3 MTPA; on the gas-processing census instead)"],"gap_decomposition":{"excluded_condensate_splitters_mtpa":24.0,"conservative_basis_understatement_mtpa":29.2,"missing_crude_refineries_mtpa":0.0},"note":"DENOMINATOR completeness (distinct from event coverage). No major crude refinery is missing: an independent open-source census maps every top-tier Russian refinery to the tracked list. The gap to the full 327 MTPA nameplate is (a) ~24 MTPA of gas-condensate splitters (Surgut CSP, Novatek Ust-Luga, Astrakhan line) that make motor fuels from CONDENSATE not crude and are excluded by the same rule as Tobolsk/ZapSibNeftekhim (6.85 MTPA, the only petrochemical exclusion); and (b) ~29 MTPA because the tracked figures come from one consistent public source (Wikipedia bbl/d, converted) that sits ~10-15% below current nameplate. Consequence for the score: because refining exposure is a capacity SHARE (struck capacity / denominator), a UNIFORM nameplate revaluation -- scaling all tracked plants up together -- leaves the exposure essentially INVARIANT (numerator and denominator scale together); the conservative basis does not systematically bias refining exposure up or down. It mainly affects the absolute MTPA and the completeness ratio against the nameplate reference. (Only a one-sided enlargement of the denominator alone would lower the exposure, which is not what a uniform revaluation does.) The consistent single-source basis is kept deliberately rather than a mixed nameplate basis; a future pass could revalue uniformly. Belarus (Mozyr, Naftan) is correctly outside the Russian denominator.","canonical_linkage":{"denominator_refineries":34,"struck_refineries":27,"mtpa_struck":234.3,"pct_denominator_mtpa_struck":85.6,"incidents_unresolved_to_registry":["Naftan refinery (Novopolotsk)"],"note":"Identity/linkage completeness, NOT disruption coverage: how much of the tracked denominator resolves to a struck canonical refinery. Naftan (Belarus) is intentionally outside the Russian denominator."}}}